# shells — the offer-only alternative shells + prompt/plugin tooling the
# `iictl shell` chooser can switch to (PROPOSAL §5). NONE of these is baked into
# the ISO: `iictl shell set <fizsh|nushell>` and `iictl shell prompt oh-my-posh`
# install the ONE package they need online on demand (official repos via pacman,
# AUR via paru), and this curated pack lets a user grab the whole set at once
# with `iictl pack install shells` — recorded + reversible via the shared engine.
#
# The default login shell stays fish and the flagship `iictl shell set zsh` is
# fully offline (zsh/zsh-completions/zoxide are baked in goodies.list); only these
# heavier / AUR-only extras are fetched.
#meta:type shells
# nushell — a structured-data shell (official repo).
nushell
# fizsh — friendly interactive zsh with bundled highlighting/autosuggestions (AUR).
fizsh
# carapace — multi-shell completion engine the themed inits wire up when present (AUR).
carapace-bin
# oh-my-posh — the opt-in alternative prompt (`iictl shell prompt oh-my-posh`, AUR).
oh-my-posh
# zsh-antidote — system-package alternative to the vendored ~/.antidote (AUR).
zsh-antidote
